From c1b80554a6dd710dcc4c81586db310909b62f5e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 22:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix discarded const qualifier from strchr in bsd-base64.c

GCC 15 / glibc 2.40+ propagate const-ness through strchr() per the
C23 type-generic forms, so passing a const char * returns a
const char *. Base64 is static const char Base64[], so the result
of strchr(Base64, ch) is const char *. Storing it in a plain
char *pos now trips -Werror=discarded-qualifiers.

Promote pos to const char *. Every use site does pointer arithmetic
with Base64 (also const), so const-correctness is fine.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
---
 src/support/bsd-base64.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/support/bsd-base64.c b/src/support/bsd-base64.c
index cb37b30..0854761 100644
--- a/src/support/bsd-base64.c
+++ b/src/support/bsd-base64.c
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ int base64url_encode(u_char const *src, size_t srclength, char *target,
 int b64_pton(char const *src, u_char *target, size_t targsize)
 {
 	int tarindex, state, ch;
-	char *pos;
+	const char *pos;
 
 	state = 0;
 	tarindex = 0;
-- 
2.53.0

